  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/691ca877-a602-4316-bd3b-24d782b1982d.png\" style=\"width:2.35347in;height:1.38681in\" /><br />As <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then by Rolle’s theorem, we get,&nbsp;<br /><math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> <math><mo>⇒</mo></math> for some <math><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> &amp; <math><msub><mrow><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Again, applying Rolle’s theorem to function <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>'</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math></p><p>we have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>\"</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>c</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> for some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Hence, the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>\"</mo></msup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> has at least one root.</p>",
